      grammar:{title:"建议、义务与程度表达", goal:"在健康类 Task 2 与口语中准确区分 should、need to、have to、may 和 tend to。", rows:[["should + 动词原形","建议，不表示强制","Governments should provide clear nutrition advice."],["need to + 动词原形","必要性，主语可为人或事物","People need to develop healthier routines."],["have to + 动词原形","外部规则或不得不","Patients may have to attend regular check-ups."],["may / can + 动词原形","可能性或能力","A sedentary lifestyle may increase health risks."],["tend to + 动词原形","一般趋势，不是绝对","People tend to exercise less when they work long hours."]], error:"❌ People should to exercise.  ✅ People should exercise.\n❌ Obesity can to cause problems.  ✅ Obesity can cause problems.", exercise:"1. Long working hours make exercise difficult.（用 may）\n2. Schools provide healthy meals.（用 should）\n3. People with little free time exercise less.（用 tend to）", answer:"1. Long working hours may make exercise difficult.\n2. Schools should provide healthy meals.\n3. People with little free time tend to exercise less."},
      listening:{title:"Section 1｜健身中心会员登记", scenario:"日常服务场景。正式考试 Listening Part 1 常见为两人对话；先读题并预测姓名、数字、日期或名词。", questions:["1. The joining fee is £______. ","2. The monthly membership costs £______.","3. The beginner class is held on ______ evenings.","4. Members need to bring a ______ for the swimming pool."], text:"Receptionist: The joining fee is fifteen pounds, and the monthly membership is thirty-two pounds. The beginner fitness class takes place on Tuesday evenings at six. If you would like to use the pool, please bring your own towel. Lockers are available, but you need a one-pound coin for the key.", answer:"15；32；Tuesday；towel。", substitution:"joining fee = fee to become a member；takes place = is held；bring your own = take with you。", task:"先遮住答案完成填空；再听读两遍，圈出价格、日期和物品。最后用 3 句复述会员信息。"},
      reading:{title:"Matching Information｜公共健康项目", type:"题型提示：题目问的是“哪一段包含某条具体信息”，重点找信息位置，不必概括整段主旨。", passage:["A  A city health department has introduced free weekend walking groups in several neighbourhood parks. Local volunteers lead routes of different lengths, so older residents and beginners can choose a suitable pace.","B  A separate programme works with supermarkets. It places simple labels beside common foods and provides recipe cards that show how to prepare low-cost meals with less salt and sugar.","C  At local workplaces, employers can apply for small grants to buy standing desks or organise short activity breaks. The project is designed for people whose jobs involve long periods of sitting.","D  Health clinics now send text-message reminders to patients who miss regular health checks. The messages also include a link to book another appointment."], questions:["1. a project intended for people with sedentary jobs", "2. help for people who want to choose food more carefully", "3. a system that contacts people after they fail to attend", "4. an activity with options for different physical abilities"], answer:"1 C；2 B；3 D；4 A。定位词：sitting → sedentary；labels/recipes → choose food；miss checks → fail to attend；different lengths/pace → different abilities。"},
      writing:{title:"Academic Task 1｜折线图：运动频率变化", prompt:"下图显示 2000、2010 和 2020 年某城市成年人每周进行三次及以上运动的比例。概括主要特征并比较。", table:[["群体","2000","2010","2020"],["18–29 岁","42%","48%","55%"],["30–49 岁","35%","38%","44%"],["50+ 岁","20%","26%","33%"]], plan:"Introduction：改写图表主题。Overview：三个年龄组均上升；18–29 岁始终最高；50+ 增幅最大。Body：先写 18–29 与 30–49，再写 50+ 的起点和终点。", band:"The proportion of adults aged 18–29 who exercised regularly rose steadily from 42% to 55%. By comparison, the figure for those aged 50 and over increased by 13 percentage points.", task:"写 1 句 introduction、1 句 overview 和 3 句比较。不要解释‘为什么’人们更常运动。"},
      speaking:{title:"Part 1｜Health and Exercise", questions:["Do you do any exercise?", "What do people in your area do to stay healthy?", "Do you think people today have healthier lifestyles than in the past?"], structure:"直接回答 → 原因 → 具体例子。避免只说 Yes, I do；至少补充一个频率、地点或习惯。", sample:"Yes, I try to exercise three times a week, usually by walking briskly after work. It helps me reduce stress, and it is easier to maintain than a complicated fitness routine.", task:"选择其中两题录音，每题 30–40 秒。回听时标出一个连接词和一个健康词汇。"},
      ece:{zh:"幼儿的 wellbeing 不只是身体健康，也包括安全感、情绪表达、休息和与他人的积极关系。教师先观察孩子的状态，再提供恰当支持。", en:"Wellbeing includes children's physical health, emotional security, rest and positive relationships. Teachers observe how a child is feeling and respond with appropriate support.", terms:[["emotional regulation","情绪调节","帮助儿童识别、表达并逐步管理情绪"],["secure relationship","安全关系","稳定、可回应的成人关系"],["calm-down space","平静角","可短暂休息、整理情绪的安静区域"]], scenario:"A child becomes upset when another child takes a toy. 练习：I noticed that… / The child may have felt… / I would support the child by…"}
