        ["conservation","n. /ˌkɒnsəˈveɪʃn/","保护；节约","wildlife conservation / water conservation","Conservation requires long-term planning.","Water conservation is essential in regions affected by drought.","conserve 是动词：节约、保护。","Conservation of ______ is important because ______."],
        ["renewable","adj. /rɪˈnjuːəbl/","可再生的","renewable energy / renewable source","Solar power is a renewable source of energy.","Governments can reduce emissions by investing in renewable energy.","反义：non-renewable。","______ is a renewable alternative to ______."],
        ["consumption","n. /kənˈsʌmpʃn/","消费；消耗","energy consumption / reduce consumption","Energy consumption rises in cold weather.","Household energy consumption can be reduced through better insulation.","来自 consume；常作不可数。","The consumption of ______ has increased because ______."],
        ["regulation","n. /ˌreɡjuˈleɪʃn/","法规；管理；调节","environmental regulation / strict regulations","Regulations can limit industrial pollution.","Environmental regulations may encourage companies to use cleaner technology.","rule 是日常规则，regulation 更正式。","Stricter regulations could reduce ______."]
